(module LED_SK6812MINI-E_ReverseMount_3.2x2.8mm (layer F.Cu) (tedit 68EB0000)
  (descr "OPSCO SK6812MINI-E reverse-mount RGB LED (LCSC C5149201), 3.2 x 2.8 x 1.78 mm. AUTHORED 2026-10-12 from studio/press/references/components/key-switches/sk6812mini-e-akizuki-rev04.pdf (OPSCO SPC/SK6812MINI-E Rev.04, PDF page 4: section 4 mechanical dimensions, section 5 pins, section 6 recommended PCB). ORIGIN is the OPTICAL CENTRE (centre of the 3.2 x 2.8 body / lens). FACE: place on the board face OPPOSITE the light direction: light exits through the Edge.Cuts cutout to the far side. As authored (F.Cu) the light goes toward the BACK of the board, so pads are drawn as the datasheet BOTTOM VIEW (pin 1 top-right, 4 top-left, 2 bottom-right, 3 bottom-left); for light toward the FRONT place the footprint on B.Cu. SOURCED: pads 1.80 x 0.82, gap between pad rows 0.68 (row centres +/-0.75), pads abut the body edge (inner edge at x=+/-1.6, total width 5.88 = 3.2 + 2 x 1.34); cutout 3.2 x 2.8; pin 1 VDD, 2 DOUT, 3 GND, 4 DIN; tolerance +/-0.1. Cutout is Edge.Cuts inside the footprint with all four corners rounded because JLCPCB does not support rectangular holes/slots without rounded corners (references/fab/jlcpcb-capabilities/jlcpcb-pcb-capabilities.txt). UNSOURCED: corner radius 0.5 (inference: min non-plated slot width 1.0 so router bit >= 1.0 dia); it clips the square body corners by ~0.15 mm diagonal and the datasheet's chamfered corner (near pin 3, mirrored here to bottom-left) is not reproduced; the sourced pads touch/overlap the rounded cutout edge by ~0.06 mm at their outer corners; courtyard; silkscreen omitted.")
  (tags "LED SK6812MINI-E RGB reverse mount C5149201 cutout")
  (fp_text reference REF** (at 0 -3.2) (layer F.SilkS)
    (effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15)))
  )
